@meeting talk.raman
// SW2, 0.92.6 item 13 (FX17's word list): a small Wren talk, 19:00-19:40 on the auditorium stage (a ring of eight
// chairs, house dark, the stars behind, tea from the kettle). Day 57, Monday. Dev Raman, Senior Helm Officer.
title: Flying like it might spill
from: Dev Raman
gist: Raman's small talk on flying the Wren gently, learnt on a noisy cargo hauler.
== lines
raman: Good evening. Please, sit. I'm used to stars in front of me, not people.   [gesture]
raman: People say I fly the Wren like she might spill. They're right. I do.   [nod]
raman: I learnt on a cargo hauler. Noisy. On every turn the crates shouted at me.
raman: So now I turn the Wren like I'm carrying soup up a ladder. Slowly. Nobody's tea moves.
raman: Twenty years, and not one cup spilt on the bridge. Well. One. It was mine.   [laugh]
raman: Before a long turn I look at my model of the Wren. Just to remember how big she is.
raman: That's all I know, really. Fly gently. Questions, if you like.
? choice
* Can a junior try the helm?   rel:raman+2 flavour:practical mem:talk.raman.asked
  raman: The simulator, yes. We'll start with a cup of water on the console.   [laugh]
* What's the hardest turn you've flown?   rel:raman+2 flavour:listen mem:talk.raman.asked
  raman: Through the dust at the Line, with Chef's soup on in the galley. Not one drop. She checked.   [laugh]
* (Just listen)
  raman: Thank you for listening so quietly. That's how I like the bridge, too.
raman: Good night, everyone. Mind your cups.
